  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Shower and thunderstorm activity will continue each afternoon \n   through early next week.\n\n-  Warming and drying latter part of next week under a ridge of\n   high pressure.\n\n\nEven though a ridge of high pressure is trying to build over the\narea today a very subtle disturbance will move through the region\nkicking off another round of showers and thunderstorms. The\ncoverage is not to be as extensive as yesterday but these storms\nwill still be capable of producing moderate to heavy rainfall,\nsmall hail and lightning. \n\nThe low amplitude ridge continues to build over the Northern\nRockies on Monday with the shower activity being fairly limited.\nThen on Tuesday, a disturbance will move into the region from\nBritish Columbia. Increased shower activity and westerly winds are\nexpected Tuesday afternoon due to this feature. \n\nThen Thursday into Friday a ridge of high pressure builds over the\nregion causing a warming and drying trend. Temperatures on Friday\nshould be in the mid 80s to mid 90s across western Montana, while\nthe lower valleys of north central Idaho reaching the century mark\nagain. These temperatures are around 10 degrees above average for\nthis time of year.",
